WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.344
Young Wu Zetian entered the palace as a Cairen (talent lady); clever and quick, she was skilled at reading people's expressions.

00:00:07.694 --> 00:00:13.694
Step by step she rose to the position of empress, handling the affairs of state together with Emperor Gaozong.

00:00:14.044 --> 00:00:19.300
Many important decisions were ones they worked out together.

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:24.594
After Gaozong passed away, she governed from behind the curtain, holding the highest power in fact.

00:00:24.944 --> 00:00:31.256
In the year 690, Wu Zetian formally proclaimed herself emperor and founded the Wu Zhou dynasty.

00:00:31.606 --> 00:00:36.598
She changed the dynastic name to Zhou and became a female emperor in Chinese history.

00:00:36.948 --> 00:00:42.732
During her reign she valued talented people, kept the court stable, and showed outstanding ability in governing the country.

00:00:43.082 --> 00:00:48.818
Under her rule, the country stayed stable and the economy kept growing.

00:00:49.168 --> 00:00:58.312
Wu Zetian was the only woman in Chinese history to formally reign as emperor, and she became one of the most famous figures of the Tang dynasty.

